# Normalize every text file to LF in the index and in the working tree, on
# every platform. Git's Windows default (core.autocrlf=true) otherwise checks
# text out as CRLF, and assets that binaries embed with `include_str!` are
# compiled in byte-for-byte: crates/pipette-ops/src/prompt_seed.txt did exactly
# that, and the CRLF seed bisected to a different 8192-token prompt that the
# server rejected, so a Windows-built client failed a benchmark that the same
# revision passed everywhere else.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Batch files are the one thing cmd.exe wants as CRLF, and they are stored that
# way. `-text` rather than `text eol=crlf`: the stored bytes are already CRLF,
# so converting on checkout would only leave android/Pipette/gradlew.bat
# permanently dirty. No binary embeds one, so passing the bytes through keeps
# them identical on every platform, which is all this file is here to do.
*.bat -text
*.cmd -text

# Stays last: `-text` has to win over the `*` rule above.
crates/pipette-llamacpp/vendor/toybox/toybox-aarch64 filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
